To create a favorite shortcut (menu or dock launcher) in Debian for `/opt/4rji/bin/digi-techsupport.AppImage`, create a `.desktop` file:


sudo mv dist/digi-techsupport-1.0.0.AppImage /opt/4rji/bin/digi-techsupport.AppImage
sudo cp build/icon.png /usr/share/icons/digi-techsupport.png

```bash
nano ~/.local/share/applications/digi-techsupport.desktop
```

Content:

```ini
[Desktop Entry]
Name=Digi TechSupport
Exec=/opt/4rji/bin/digi-techsupport.AppImage
Icon=digi-techsupport
Type=Application
Categories=Utility;
Terminal=false
```

**Quick notes:**

* Make sure the AppImage has execute permissions: `chmod +x /opt/4rji/bin/digi-techsupport.AppImage`
* The `digi-techsupport` icon must be in `/usr/share/icons`, or use an absolute path if you have a PNG or SVG, for example: `Icon=/opt/4rji/bin/digi-techsupport.png`
* Then you can search for it in the menu and pin it.
